  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Identify the following surface:\n\n$$\n{z}^{2}=8x,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty .\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that the equation of a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py.\n$$\n\nThus, a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $y$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n{z}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $y$-axis and $p=2.$",
